# Minimal NEP training input (GPUMD >= 4.x "nep" executable, NEP4 only)
# Reads train.xyz (and test.xyz if present) from the current directory.
# Keyword reference: https://gpumd.org/nep/input_files/nep_in.html
#
# Mandatory: number of species and their symbols (order = order in nep.txt)
type          2 Mo S
version       4            # the only accepted value in current GPUMD
# Radial / angular cutoffs in Angstrom (default 8 4; 3 <= angular <= radial <= 10)
cutoff        6 4
# Descriptor and network size (documented defaults written out)
n_max         6 6
basis_size    6 6
l_max         4 1
neuron        30
# Loss weights (defaults); lambda_v 0 if your DFT data have no reliable stress
lambda_e      1.0
lambda_f      1.0
lambda_v      0.1
# SNES optimiser (defaults are batch 1000, population 50, generation 100000).
# A short first run to check the data pipeline; raise generation for production.
batch         1000
population    50
generation    20000
# Uncomment to evaluate an existing nep.txt on train.xyz/test.xyz instead of training:
# prediction  1
